<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of verse, one column, with a running head at the top left and a page number at the top right. Below the text, at the right, a gathering mark.</layout>
  <page_number>51</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIAC A.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>D. ij</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Vidit carnificis brachia Guisii</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Non una immeriti cæde rubentia.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Et dixit: Nemesis, vindice dextera</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Pœnas commeritas exiget horrida</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Cædis, cæde tua, cum veniet dies.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Hic multas sed enim iam prius hauserat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Illustres animas, illius æmulus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Qui venator atrox dicitur: opprimens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Immani rabie non aliter pios,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Quam saltu celeres in medio feras.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Quam longè Morini Phocaica procul</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Abfunt Massylia, Mosáq; Cantabris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Tam longè posuit post etiam plagas,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>In quas, Romulicum qui renuunt nefas,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Et Christi cupiunt vocibus obsequi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Illapsi ruerent irremeabiles.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Heu quas inde neces pertulit innocens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Coetus, Christe tibi deditus!</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>(haec seges</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Quæ semper studuit crescere honoribus)</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Et sylvæ, &amp; fluvij montibus addit-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>i Norunt, dum vacuis urbibus audiunt</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Effusos gemitus auia per loca</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Lugentúmque globos diffugientium.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Novit, barbariem suspiciens suam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Deuictam Oceanus, barbarie nova,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Dum passim profugos excipiens pio</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Anglorum properat reddere luttori[?]:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" para="true">
      <i>Anglorum hospitibus nunc ita lenium,</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed "Guifii" read as Guisii, long s taken as s. "Mofáq;" is uncertain: the mark after the q is a small abbreviation sign and may not be a plain q;. "luttori" is uncertain and marked [?]. The ornamental marks before "Anglorum" are decoration, not text. The underlining under "Quàm" and "Quam" is not transcribed. The faint text in the right margin is show-through and is left out.</notes>
</page>
